---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Direct-mapped-8: 0x000 and 0x080 share set 0, its only way, so each load evicts the other (cases 2 and 3). The first two misses are compulsory; the return of 0x000 is a conflict, since a fully associative cache of eight lines would still hold it."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x000: tag 0x00, set 0, offset 0 (word 0).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 0 is invalid. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Set 0 has one way; the line goes there.
1.4 | fill | lineSize | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x000–0x00F from memory.
1.5 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 0 of way 0 (5) into r1.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x080: tag 0x01, set 0, offset 0 (word 0).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, compulsory | - | Set 0 holds tag 0x00, not 0x01. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
2.4 | evict | associativity | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x000 (tag 0x00) from way 0.
2.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x080–0x08F from memory.
2.6 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 0 of way 0 (33) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | - | Load 0x000: tag 0x00, set 0, offset 0 (word 0).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, conflict | - | Set 0 holds tag 0x01, not 0x00. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | - | Direct-mapped: way 0 is the only place for this line, so its current line must go.
3.4 | evict | associativity | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, evictions | - | Evict line 0x080 (tag 0x01) from way 0.
3.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 0/0, tag 0/0, word 0/0/0, word 0/0/1, word 0/0/2, word 0/0/3, fills | - | Fill way 0 with line 0x000–0x00F from memory.
3.6 | complete | - | r1 | - | Read word 0 of way 0 (5) into r1.
